# Stepping stones: a stroke becomes a footpath spline in the ground_edit, a
# line of stones a stride apart (0.6-0.8 m) down its middle, slightly
# zig-zagged, turned along it and bedded in; the ground is not flattened, the
# grass is only worn between the stones, and a little earth shows. Across a
# river the stones carry on as a ford, their tops above the water.
# docs/guide/36-terrain-paint.md "Paths".
# Poly Haven (CC0): dirt_floor, rock_moss_set_02 (the stones).
name: Stepping stones
doc: A line of stepping stones a stride apart, the grass worn between them; they carry on across water as a ford.
order: 112
path:
  style: stepping_stones
  width_scale: 1
  simplify: 0.3
  flatten: false
  shape: {wear: 0.8, edge: 0.35, stride: 0.7}
recipe:
  textures:
    - {name: path_dirt, id: dirt_floor, scale: 2.5}
  material:
    - {mask: path_wear, texture: path_dirt, slots: [wet, ash, snow], fallback: cracked, strength: 0.35}
    - {mask: path_stepping_stones, texture: path_dirt, slots: [wet, ash, snow], fallback: cracked, strength: 0.6}
  exclude:
    - {mask: path_wear, kind: grass_field, shrink: 0.6}
    - {mask: path_clear, kind: scatter}
  stages:
    - stage: polyhaven_rocks
      id: path_rocks_src
      params:
        assets: [{id: rock_moss_set_02}]
        back: none
    - stage: ground_edit
      id: ground_edit
      params:
        terrain: $source
        path_rocks: path_rocks_src
